carlos-ctl (1.1.2~dev1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * import-o19 now takes the database-ownership lock
    (/var/lib/carlos-emr/.finish-install.lock) that carlos-emr's and
    carlos-emr-drugref's configure, carlos-emr-provision.service and
    finish-install already share, before it writes its ledger, and holds
    it until it exits (carlos-emr/carlos#3678). Previously the importer
    only became visible to those paths' o19 guard once its ledger was
    published, leaving a window in which a configure or boot repair could
    restart MariaDB, rewrite grants or run Flyway under the copy. Every
    mode except an assessment takes it (a real run, --resume, --cleanup,
    --dry-run); an import started while a provisioning run holds it is
    refused with nothing written.
  * The dev snapshot version: release builds stamp the tag's version.

 -- CARLOS EMR Maintainers <michael@maplecreekmedical.ca>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000

